WEBVTT

00:00:00.556 --> 00:00:02.606
Substitution changes letters.

00:00:03.266 --> 00:00:05.096
Transposition moves them.

00:00:05.546 --> 00:00:09.116
The alphabet stays the same,
only the order changes.

00:00:10.956 --> 00:00:14.386
Transposition rearranges
the order of characters.

00:00:15.146 --> 00:00:17.096
The character set stays identical,

00:00:17.566 --> 00:00:20.016
so the frequency profile is preserved.

00:00:21.889 --> 00:00:23.119
Rail-fence cipher.

00:00:23.804 --> 00:00:26.494
Write plaintext in a zigzag across rails,

00:00:26.924 --> 00:00:28.594
then read row by row.

00:00:29.099 --> 00:00:33.699
Plaintext meetmeafterthetogaparty
with 3 rails becomes

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:36.099
mmthgretfeteoaateartpy.

00:00:37.522 --> 00:00:39.072
Columnar transposition.

00:00:39.717 --> 00:00:42.187
Write rows of fixed
length under a keyword,

00:00:42.737 --> 00:00:45.687
then read columns in the
keyword's letter order.

00:00:46.162 --> 00:00:48.652
The keyword determines the permutation.

00:00:50.422 --> 00:00:51.752
Double transposition.

00:00:52.387 --> 00:00:55.837
Apply columnar transposition
twice with two keys.

00:00:56.447 --> 00:00:58.477
Much stronger than a single pass.

00:01:00.256 --> 00:01:02.406
Transposition creates diffusion.

00:01:03.091 --> 00:01:07.521
Each plaintext digit influences
many ciphertext digits.

00:01:08.146 --> 00:01:12.216
Shannon's property of diffusion
is achieved by permutation.

